course: dictionary
lesson: 1720
title: Cloud words
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Scientists and weather forecasters name clouds by their shape and height. When you meet an unknown cloud word, use its context: the words and sentences around it give clues. «Cirrus clouds are thin wispy clouds of ice high in the sky.» Thin, wispy and high up tells you cirrus is a kind of cloud that is not heavy or low.
explain: The sentence in the notes gives more clues: «cumulus are white puffy heaps of fair weather; stratus are flat grey sheets that may bring drizzle; cirrus are thin wisps of ice high up.» Each name is paired with a shape and a height, so you can compare them. Cumulus is puffy and stratus is flat, so cirrus must be the thin, wispy one.
explain: Cirrus can also be a clue about tomorrow's weather. Cirrus often means fair weather, but it can show that the weather will change within a day or so. Always test your meaning in the sentence: if «cirrus clouds» means thin wispy clouds of ice high up, the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Cirrus is a noun. The plural is cirri.
fact: «Cirrus» means a thin, wispy, white cloud high up in the sky, made of tiny ice crystals.
fact: Cirrus clouds can look like feathers or horses' tails.
fact: Cirrus often means fair weather, but it can show that the weather will change in a day or so.
fact: The word comes from Latin for a curl of hair.
exercise: «Cirrus clouds are thin wispy clouds of ice high in the sky.» What are cirrus clouds made of? | Hot steam from the sea | Grey dust from the road | *Tiny ice crystals | Heavy rain
exercise: «A cumulonimbus is a towering storm cloud that brings heavy rain, thunder and sometimes hail.» Which cloud is this? | Cirrus | Cumulus | *Cumulonimbus | Stratus
exercise: Cirrus clouds can look like what? | Bricks stacked in a wall | Flat stones on a beach | *Feathers or horses' tails | Thick black blankets
exercise: Cirrus clouds often mean what? | A hot, dry week for certain | Thunder right now | Heavy snow tonight | *Fair weather, but a change may come within a day or so
test: The word cirrus comes from Latin for what? | *A curl of hair | A bird's wing | A grey sheet | A storm
test: «Stratus are flat grey sheets that may bring drizzle.» Which cloud is this? | Cirrus | *Stratus | Cumulus | Cumulonimbus
exam: Which description is true of cirrus? | *Thin, wispy and high up, made of tiny ice crystals | Flat grey sheets that bring drizzle | Low, dark and full of thunder | Puffy heaps of fair weather
